(    ?The wide seas and the mountains called to him,) Tj T*
(      And grey dawn saw his camp-fires in the rain.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There are times when everyone wants to be a vagabond, and go down the) Tj T*
(road to adventure, strange peoples, the mountains, and the sea. The bonds) Tj T*
(of convention, however, are many and strong, and only a few ever break) Tj T*
(them and go.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In this book I have gathered together the strange and romantic lives of) Tj T*
(actual wanderers who did what so many have wished to do; here are some) Tj T*
(who gave up all to go and see the world. The booming of temple gongs over) Tj T*
(the rice fields sounded in their ears, they tasted strange food cooked) Tj T*
(on charcoal fires in the twilight quiet of midocean isles, they knew the) Tj T*
(mountain wind keen with the smell of snow, the mystery of roads along) Tj T*
ET
