(great rivers, and the broad path of ships on lonely seas. Whatever was to) Tj T*
(be seen, they went to see; they did things the world thought could not) Tj T*
(be done.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Life is a kind of book which is put into our hands with many pages still) Tj T*
(uncut; some are content with the open leaves, others cut a few pages, the) Tj T*
(vagabond reads the whole book if he can.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I have called these wanderers ?Gallant Vagabonds? to separate them from) Tj T*
(both the professional travellers and the vagabond ne?er-do-wells. The) Tj T*
(gallant vagabond is not the man with the sun helmet and the file of) Tj T*
(native bearers; nor is he the wastrel who drifts down-stream and sees) Tj T*
(the world as he goes; the real prince of vagabonds is the wayfarer with) Tj T*
(scarce a penny in his pocket who fights his way upstream to see where the) Tj T*
(river rises, and crosses the dark mountains to find the fabled town. His) Tj T*
(curiosity is never purely geographical, it lies in the whole fantastic) Tj T*
(mystery of life.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The true gallant vagabond is one of the heroes of humanity, and history) Tj T*
(owes him many of her great discoveries, many of her most spirited and) Tj T*
(romantic episodes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Here you will find, gathered in their own vagabond company, John Ledyard) Tj T*
(the runaway college sophomore who thought of walking round the world,) Tj T*
(Belzoni the monk who became an acrobat and then an archæologist, Edward) Tj T*
(John Trelawny, the deserter, pirate, and country gentleman who came) Tj T*
(so mysteriously into the life of Shelley; Thomas Morton, the jovial) Tj T*
(Elizabethan who scandalized the New England Puritans with a Mayday revel,) Tj T*
(Arthur Rimbaud the poet who became an African trader, and James Bruce the) Tj T*
(sturdy Scot who rose to be a great lord in Abyssinia. The accounts are) Tj T*
(authentic, and if they seem like fiction, the reader must call to mind) Tj T*
(the old adage about the strangeness of the truth.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
