(warriors.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Ellar the comedian knew him well, and saw him perform; the giant was) Tj T*
(getting two pounds a week, and Edmund Kean was watching delighted in the) Tj T*
(stalls.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In England came Romance: there Gianbattista found his Sarah. This) Tj T*
(resolute spouse was an Englishwoman of a stature almost as magnificent) Tj T*
(as her lord?s, and with a character and a mind as British as the dome of) Tj T*
(St. Paul?s. Indomitable Sarah Belzoni! Writing of the Turks, she set down) Tj T*
(in her journal, ?though I may be condemned for my opinion, there is no) Tj T*
(religion would suit them so well as the Protestant church of England.?) Tj T*
(She called her husband ?Mr. B.,? and accompanied him on his expeditions,) Tj T*
